  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The target alloy has a multiphase eutectic microstructure containing distinct FCC and intermetallic or sigma-type phases.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::006::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The alloy naturally forms compositionally heterogeneous protective oxide films.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9319277::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heterogeneous phase distributions create local galvanic cells at interphase boundaries.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::006::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Elevated temperature destabilizes the alloy's passive oxide film.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9319277::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mechanical wear continually removes passive films and exposes fresh metal.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Passive films are thinner or more non-uniform at phase boundaries.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Electrochemical potential differences between phases drive micro-galvanic corrosion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::006::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Micro-galvanic corrosion undermines the alloy's wear resistance.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Repeated passive-film breakage and reformation creates a positive feedback loop between mechanical and chemical degradation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The positive feedback loop accelerates both wear and corrosion under simultaneous exposure.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to a single-phase or compositionally homogeneous baseline, the multiphase alloy will have a higher total degradation rate.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::006::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to the baseline, the multiphase alloy will show a moderate increase in wear because of more frequent oxide spallation.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to the baseline, the multiphase alloy will show a significant increase in corrosion rate because of intensified galvanic interactions.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12156342::web::006::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A chloride-containing sulfuric acid solution can produce an unstable passive film on a eutectic high-entropy alloy at high temperature.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9319277::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "At low temperature, the passive film can remain stable in the chloride-containing sulfuric acid solution.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9319277::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "A substantially milder corrosive environment or a temperature too low to destabilize the film will suppress the proposed accelerated-degradation mechanism.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9319277::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    }
